  "question": {
    "text": "If the function \\(f:(-\\infty, \\infty) \\rightarrow B\\) defined by \\(f(x)=-x^2+6 x-8\\) is bijective, then \\(B=\\)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "gkZBr",
      "text": "\\([1, \\infty)\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lzFUS",
      "text": "\\((-\\infty, 1]\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "9mgUH",
      "text": "\\((-\\infty, \\infty)\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "skSNt",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since the function \\(f\\) is bijective, therefore \\(f\\) is onto. Therefore range of \\(f=B\\).\nLet \\(y=-x^2+6 x-8\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}^2-6 \\mathrm{x}+(8+\\mathrm{y})=0\\)\n\\(\\Rightarrow x=\\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{36-4(8+y)}}{2}=\\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{4-4 y}}{2}\\)\nFor \\(x\\) to be real, \\(4-4 y \\geq 0 \\Rightarrow y \\leq 1\\)\n\\(\\therefore \\mathrm{B}=\\) range of \\(\\mathrm{F}=(-\\infty, 1]\\)",
    "image": null
  },
